======================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
======================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - Binary distress (primary H4): Score≥3 17.1% vs Score≤1 12.6%; χ²=8.04, p=0.005; Fisher OR=1.44.
      => SUPPORTED — StressScore is a working distress flag.
  - Continuous ΔGM (v9 UPDATE): High-Low ΔGM=-0.56pp, t=-3.64, p=0.000.
      => REVERSED from v8: now significant. StressScore separates continuous margins too (not flag-only).
  - Monotonicity: Distress rate rises monotonically 11.7%→13.7%→15.7%→17.1%, then plateaus at Score 4 (17.1%).
      => Clean ordinal gradient; no dip. Supports the score as a stress measure.
  - By super-group: NO super-group significant at 5% (closest: Technology p=0.07, Materials p=0.10).
      => Per-group underpowered; the pooled chi-square is the only reportable distress result.
  - F1-F4 component decomposition: Underlying flags NOT stored in the v9 panel; component tables omitted.
      => Honestly dropped — would require fabricating data. Rebuild from raw if needed.
  - US-share: High-stress firms span all groups; tech/healthcare most US-heavy (79%/71%).
      => Stress flag is broad-based, not a US-only construct.
  - Independence from H1 (CRITICAL): StressScore correlates 0.62 with AbnInvPeer AND its outcome (ΔGM) is the H1 outcome.
      => Phase 9 is NOT independent corroboration of the inventory→margin link: it shares both the predictor (partly) and the outcome with H1. Report as mechanism illustration, not separate evidence.

